SUMMARY:AYPROS Government Relations Crew: October Meeting with Mayoral Can
 didates  
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Young Professionals (AYPROS)\nLocal government decis
 ions shape nearly every part of life in Asheville\, from housing and trans
 portation to economic development\, public safety\, parks\, and the future
  of downtown. Understanding how those decisions are made\, and where resid
 ents can have a meaningful voice\, is not always as straightforward.\n\nJo
 in the AYPROS Government Relations Crew for our October meeting as we cont
 inue creating a place where young professionals can better understand loca
 l government\, discuss the issues affecting our region\, and become more i
 nformed and involved in the future of Asheville and Buncombe County.\n\nTh
 is month\, we are pleased to welcome **Asheville City Mayor Esther Manheim
 er and City Councilor and Mayoral Candidate Kim Roney.**\n\nMembers will h
 ave an opportunity to hear directly from both\, ask questions\, and contri
 bute their own perspectives to the conversation.\n\n## What You Can Expect
 \n\nEach month\, the Government Relations Crew gathers for a focused\, wor
 king-style discussion covering current issues affecting Asheville and Bunc
 ombe County.\n\nThroughout the year\, Crew members will also have opportun
 ities to:\n\n* Hear from community leaders\, elected officials\, planners\
 , and policy experts\n* Attend City Council and other public meetings toge
 ther\n* Organize around initiatives that align with AYPROS’ mission\n* T
 ake field visits to better understand projects and community issues firsth
 and\n* Help continue building programs such as 828 Lead\, 828 Vote\, and A
 YPROS Day at the Capitol\n\nOur goal is not to advocate from assumptions. 
 It is to become informed\, thoughtful leaders who can positively influence
  our community.\n\n## Who Should Attend\n\nThe Government Relations Crew i
 s open to any AYPROS member who wants to better understand local governmen
 t\, public policy\, and the issues affecting our community.\nWhether you a
 re already civically engaged\, work in a related field\, or are simply cur
 ious about how decisions get made\, you are welcome to join us. No prior e
 xperience is required\, and first-time attendees are encouraged to partici
 pate.\n\n## Calling All 828 Lead Graduates\n\nBring your **828 Lead binder
 **\, wear your **828 Lead pin** if you have one\, and represent your cohor
 t. This is a chance to put what you learned into practice and continue bui
 lding your understanding of local leadership and government.\n\n## Event D
 etails\n\n**Monday\, September 14\, 2026**\n**9:00 AM - 10:00 AM**\n\nHatc
 hworks Coworking\n45 S. French Broad Avenue\, Suite 170\nAsheville\, NC 28
 801\n\nIf you are interested in helping shape the future of Asheville whil
 e spending time with other engaged young professionals\, we would be glad 
 to have you join us.\n\nPlease register so we know you are coming.\n\nCoff
 ee will be provided!
