SUMMARY:AYPROS All Access 2026  
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Young Professionals (AYPROS)\nWhat would you ask som
 eone who is exactly as successful right now as you hope to be someday?\n\n
 How did you start? What was your biggest failure? What do you wish you kne
 w at 25 or 30? What decision changed everything? And what would you tell s
 omeone sitting where you are right now?\n**AYPROS All Access** is built ar
 ound those conversations.\n\nOn **Tuesday\, October 6**\, a small group of
  Asheville’s young professionals will sit at the table with eight accomp
 lished founders\, executives and community leaders for an evening unlike a
 nything we have done before.\nThis is not a panel. There is no keynote. Yo
 u will not spend the night sitting in rows listening to someone speak from
  a stage.\n\nInstead\, attendees will take part in **four 20-minute small-
 group conversations**\, rotating from table to table throughout the evenin
 g. Each table will be hosted by one of our featured leaders\, giving you t
 he chance to ask questions\, hear the stories behind their successes and f
 ailures\, and have the kind of conversation most people rarely get access 
 to.\n\n### Your All Access Table Leaders\n\n**Barry E.A. Johnson**\nFormer
  Obama Administration official\, founding Executive Director of SelectUSA\
 , and longtime business and economic development leader.\n\n**Chris Heivly
 **\nCo-founder of MapQuest\, entrepreneur\, investor and former Managing D
 irector of Techstars.\n\n**Amy Daniels**\nExecutive Director of the Caroli
 na Hurricanes Foundation and longtime nonprofit and philanthropic leader.\
 n\n**Dr. Richard Furman**\nSurgeon\, entrepreneur and co-founder of World 
 Medical Mission.\n\n**Michael Ciochetti**\nEntrepreneur and developer behi
 nd one of the country’s most celebrated private fly-in communities.\n\n*
 *Rachel Sossoman**\nHealthcare executive and leader in Western North Carol
 ina.\n\n**Vic Isley**\nPresident & CEO of Explore Asheville and a national
 ly recognized tourism and destination leader.\n\n**Kwame Anku**\nFounder\,
  investor and entrepreneur working with companies and founders across the 
 country.\n\nAfter the four conversations\, the evening opens up for drinks
 \, food and time to continue the conversations that started around the tab
 les.\nAll Access is intentionally limited. The point is not to fill a ball
 room. It is to create a room where you can actually **sit across from peop
 le you admire\, ask the questions you have always wanted to ask\, and leav
 e knowing people you probably would not have known otherwise.**\n\nOne eve
 ning.\nEight leaders.\nFour conversations.\nA seat at the table.\n\n**Tues
 day\, October 6\, 2026**\n**Asheville\, NC**\nAttendance is limited.\n\n##
 # Purchase Tickets\n\nTickets are available through Zeffy:\n[https://www.z
 effy.com/en-US/ticketing/aypros-all-access--2026](https://www.zeffy.com/en
 -US/ticketing/aypros-all-access--2026)
